BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every WOTC operator hammers the same clock: the packet lives or dies inside a 28-day window. Workforce3One tells) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (employers to submit the forms within 28 days after the new employee starts working. It also warns against sending) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (them to the Internal Revenue Service or the U.S. Department of Labor in Washington, DC [w5ydUbSH5TI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (00:03:41]. SC DEW repeats the 28-calendar-day rule, measured from the start date. It lists late filings alongside rehires,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (relatives and 1099 workers as ineligible [ujWX1IZPyFc @ 00:05:22]. Nicole Larrison, the Louisiana Workforce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Commission WOTC State Program Manager, says the application must be postmarked or uploaded within 28 days of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (hire. She calls it 'an irs mandated deadline so there's no way around it' [xtpFtLZJyrM @ 00:20:41]. Jason D. Knott adds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (the second non-negotiable: the employer files a completed Form 8850 and the ETA 9061 with the state workforce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (agency, and 'you can't just send one' [RmnPUe0eO7s @ 00:08:06]. The working consensus has three parts. The two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (forms travel as one unit. The state agency is the only inbox. A packet that lands on day 29 is dead paper. SC DEW goes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (a step further and tells employers not to hold the request while waiting on supporting documentation. The same session) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (confirms there is no cap on the number of qualified hires an employer can push through [ujWX1IZPyFc @ 00:05:42].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (Outside WOTC, the agreement is just as blunt: a claim is only as strong as its paper trail. Stephanie Thomas and Eric) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Thomas of Sales Tax Sisters say the required documentation depends on the basis of the refund. The basis might be a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (client who was overcharged and reimbursed, tax overpaid on a purchase, or an error on a return. They state flatly that 'if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (you're going to go for a refund you have to be able to substantiate that the refund is due' [LibBgjGxja4 @ 00:02:50].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (Their closing takeaway is documentation, documentation, documentation, backed by an audit trail for the entire audit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (period [LibBgjGxja4 @ 00:05:34]. Rich Smith applies the same logic to energy deductions: 'The documentation is just) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (as important as the upgrade because without that 179D falls apart' [jW2x9diynM0 @ 00:05:14]. On R&D, Cherry) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (Bekaert points to the new Form 6765 Section G, which requires business-component detail covering 80% of QREs or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (the first 50 business components [IYUnmXCy8I0 @ 00:39:33]. One presenter argues the heavier disclosure is 'going to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (reduce the incidence of of audit' rather than invite more scrutiny [IYUnmXCy8I0 @ 00:32:09]. The Section 174A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (session adds two points. Qualifying activities are measured by business component, and the component counts reported) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (on the form should stay consistent from year to year [nR3lgfqRNqg @ 00:28:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (The third point of agreement is sequence. The paperwork that unlocks a benefit has to exist before the triggering event,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (and the benefit is claimed only after an outside party signs off. IRS stakeholder liaisons Anika Pampei and Cheryl) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (Jackson make three points about Form 8850. Page 2 carries four employer dates. The 'gave information' date must fall) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (on or before the 'offered' date. The whole form is signed under penalty of perjury [onLA9L1sYIc @ 00:18:03]. SC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (DEW lays out the claim order step by step: obtain certification first, verify the retention minimum, apply the wage cap,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (and only then pass the result to the CPA [ujWX1IZPyFc @ 00:07:29]. Rich Smith runs the same playbook on 179D.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (The energy model must be certified before installation, and the December phone calls arrive too late to rescue anything) Tj ET
