BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (August 2026, with payment in September to October 2026, so operators wait well over a year from the start of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (performance year before any savings check clears.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Fredrikson's gainsharing playbook puts the sharpest numbers on the table. No physician share above 50% appears in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (the advisory opinions, though higher is not categorically barred; on implant savings, $10M saved with $5M to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (physicians is arguably fine, while at 75% the speakers flatly would not do it [VMuMGmjYplc @ 00:28:18]. Metrics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (must sit inside the physicians' control: a $100,000 bonus triggered at 90% on-time starts fails at about 87% because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (anesthesia causes 8% of delays and nursing 4%, so the fix is tiers at 85, 90 and 95%, 'a rheostat rather than a light) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (switch' [VMuMGmjYplc @ 00:22:59]. Under CJR the physician cap is 50% of Medicare professional fees, so $100K) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (saved against $30K in fees pays $15K, and equal splits are not allowed [VMuMGmjYplc @ 00:43:17]. Absolute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (targets such as ten minutes faster are fine; paying for doubled OB deliveries is suspect; each group gets capped at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (historical volume. John Ford shows where the savings actually come from in an ACO: work the ED frequent-flyer list,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (where one patient dropped from 73 visits a year to the low teens for about $20,000 saved [UEDbkKJ-9Xk @ 00:13:54].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (Fredrikson's documentation rule is blunt: keep it off email, and keep device companies out entirely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (The aggressive edge comes from patient and network selection. Markovitz ran a 'reverse ACO Builder' test, inspired by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Milliman's nationwide map of high- and low-cost physicians, and found dispersed convener ACOs spending about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm ($400 below the regional benchmark versus about $100 for dispersed non-convener ACOs [Zzb5OKFwcbg @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (00:16:26]. Those dispersed convener ACOs earned roughly $171 per beneficiary per year in bonuses against about $95) Tj ET
